Looking at the crash in more detail, I inspected the contents of `PhpParser\Node\Stmt\Do_` in https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/blob/38c452ae584467e939d55377aaf83b5a26f19dd1/src/Psalm/Internal/Analyzer/StatementsAnalyzer.php#L497-L499 by adding a try-catch:

```php
        } elseif ($stmt instanceof PhpParser\Node\Stmt\Do_) {
            try {
                DoAnalyzer::analyze($statements_analyzer, [$stmt], $context);
            } catch (\Throwable $e) {
                \error_log((new PhpParser\PrettyPrinter\Standard())->prettyPrint($stmt));
                throw $e;
            }
```

The actual code in `$stmt` there is:

```php
do {
    $response = $this->client->get($this->endpoint, $batchCriteria->toArray());
    $this->requestedCriteria->limit = $this->requestedCriteria->limit ?? 0;
    /** @psalm-var list<array> $items */
    $items = ($this->collectionParser)($response);
    if ([] === $items) {
        break;
    }
    foreach ($items as $item) {
        if ($this->requestedCriteria->limit <= $fetchedItems) {
            break;
        }
        (yield $itemParser($item));
        ++$fetchedItems;
    }
    $batchCriteria->page = ++$currentPage;
} while ($this->requestedCriteria->limit > $fetchedItems);
```

The problem seems to occur because `$this->requestedCriteria` is modified within the loop, when a `break;` occurs, but I'm unsure how to reproduce the issue in isolation :thinking:
